{"id":8988217,"docketId":66254433,"caseName":"Maffei v. United States","caseNameFull":"Maffei v. United States","slug":"maffei-v-united-states","docketNumber":"No. 71-6176","dateFiled":"1972-05-15","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1972,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":4,"judges":"Douglas","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8980293,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":103,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<p id=\"AXT\">C. A. 6th</p>\n<p id=\"AInG\">Cir. Certiorari denied.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":8980294,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Douglas","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":3023,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b918-5\">Me. Justice Douglas,</author>\n<p id=\"A66\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b918-6\">Seven courts of appeals, including the court below, have held that a federal defendant who presents evidence in his behalf thereby waives any error in a prior denial of a motion for acquittal made at the close of the Government\u2019s case. <em>United States </em>v. <em>Haskell, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"263079\"><a href=\"/opinion/263079/united-states-v-jerome-j-haskell/#282\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Jerome J. Haskell\">327 F. 2d 281, 282, n. 2</a></span> (CA2); <em>United States </em>v. <em>Feldman, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"289873\"><a href=\"/opinion/289873/united-states-v-robert-feldman/#692\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Robert Feldman\">425 F. 2d 688, 692</a></span> <em>(CA3); United States </em>v. <em>Cashio, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"288114\"><a href=\"/opinion/288114/united-states-v-samuel-c-cashio/#1134\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Samuel C. Cashio\">420 F. 2d 1132, 1134</a></span> (CA5); <em>United States </em>v. <em>Carabbia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"276771\"><a href=\"/opinion/276771/united-states-v-ronald-carabbia/#138\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Ronald Carabbia\">381 F. 2d 133, 138</a></span> (CA6); <em>Cline </em>v. <em>United States, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"280247\"><a href=\"/opinion/280247/john-francis-cline-v-united-states/#144\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: John Francis Cline v. United States\">395 F. 2d 138, 144</a></span> (CA8); <em>Viramontes-Medina </em>v. <em>United States, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"285146\"><a href=\"/opinion/285146/ramon-viramontes-medina-v-united-states/#982\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ramon Viramontes-Medina v. United States\">411 F. 2d 981, 982</a></span> (CA9); <em>United States </em>v. <em>Greene, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"296753\"><a href=\"/opinion/296753/united-states-v-reico-lonnie-greene-aka-reico-l-greene/#1286\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Reico Lonnie Greene, A/K/A Reico L. Greene\">442 F. 2d 1285, 1286-1287, n. 3</a></span> (CA10). Two other courts of appeals, however, have held that presentation of a defense is not a waiver. <em>United States </em>v. <em>Rizzo, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"286695\"><a href=\"/opinion/286695/united-states-v-patrick-ralph-rizzo-aka-alfred-dale-rosenheck/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: United States v. Patrick Ralph Rizzo, A/K/A Alfred Dale...\">416 F. 2d 734</a></span>, 736 n. 3 (CA7); <em>Cephus </em>v. <em>United States, </em>117 U. S. App. D. C. 15, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9449718\"><a href=\"/opinion/262433/earl-r-cephus-v-united-states/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Earl R. Cephus v. United States\">324 F. 2d 893</a></span>. I would grant this petition to resolve the conflict. Rule 19 (1) (b) of the Rules of this Court.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}